{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>El a wadi eitan.</b> A perennial river, as in 'the mighty rivers are dried up' (הובשת נהרות איתן). And a proof for this: 'and they shall wash their hands' (ורחצו ידיהם) — [which implies a place where water flows]." "<b>Which is not worked.</b> That it had no channels to irrigate the ground adjacent to it." "<b>And shall not be sown.</b> One does not sow the ground adjacent to it." "<b>And shall not be sown.</b> By analogy to a decreed land, for both have the same meaning." "<b>And they shall break its neck.</b> Just as the slain man had his neck broken." "<b>The heifer.</b> A sign and symbol: just as the heifer is whole and clean, having done nothing, and the ground is virgin ground, so too we are clean of the bloodshed."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:34.491070541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}